# Tips shown one-at-a-time on each new interactive shell.
# One tip per line; lines starting with # are ignored, as are blank lines.
# Edit freely — just push and it propagates to every box overnight.

# ── core CLI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tldr <cmd> — instant offline cheat-sheet for any command. Try `tldr tar`.
xh GET httpbin.org/headers — friendlier curl. Use ":=" for raw JSON, "==" for query params.
cd foo — zoxide aliased to `cd`; type a frecent fragment, no full path needed.
zi — zoxide interactive: fuzzy-pick from your visited dirs.
bat <file> — cat with syntax highlighting + git markers. Set `--paging=never` for piping.
eza -lah --git --icons — better ls; `l` and `ll` are pre-aliased.
fd <pattern> — sane `find`. Respects .gitignore by default.
rg <pattern> — ripgrep; faster than grep, ignores .git, respects .gitignore.
fzf — Ctrl+T to pick a file, Ctrl+R for history (via atuin), Alt+C to fuzzy-cd.
jq '.foo.bar' — JSON filter/pretty-print. `jq -r` for raw output.
yq '.foo.bar' — same as jq, for YAML/TOML.
btop — modern htop. Press `h` once for the keybind cheat-sheet.
mkcd foo — mkdir + cd in one go (zsh function).
serve — alias for `python3 -m http.server`; quick HTTP server in cwd.
myip — alias for `curl -s ifconfig.me`.
dco — alias for `docker compose`. `dps` for a pretty docker ps.

# ── git ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gs — git status. gd — diff. gp — push. gl — pull. gco — checkout. gcm — commit -m.
glog — git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all. The "where am I" command.
lazygit (or `lzg`) — TUI for git. Easier than memorising flags for any non-trivial rebase.
delta — already wired in as your git pager; use `git diff` and it's prettier than diff-so-fancy.
git wip — alias: `git add -A && git commit -m wip --no-verify`. Useful before a risky pull.
git pushf — alias for `push --force-with-lease`. Safer than `--force`.
git sync — alias: `pull --rebase && push`. The "catch me up" command.
gh pr create --fill — opens a PR using the last commit message as title+body.
gh pr checkout 123 — fetches a PR and checks it out as a local branch.
gh dash — TUI dashboard for every PR / issue / repo on your account.

# ── dotfiles / chezmoi ─────────────────────────────────────────────
chezmoi update — pull main + apply. Otherwise the 03:17 timer does it nightly.
chezmoi edit ~/.zshrc — edit the source template, not the live file.
chezmoi diff — preview what would change before applying.
chezmoi managed — list every file chezmoi controls. `unmanaged` for the inverse.
chezmoi data — show resolved template variables (os, hostname, prompts).
~/.local/bin/dotfiles-brew-sync — push your local brew installs into the Brewfile now (else 02:00 nightly).

# ── runtimes / env ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
mise use -g node@lts — install + set the global default for any tool.
mise use node@20.11 — set a project-local pin (writes .mise.toml in cwd).
mise install — install everything pinned in .mise.toml.
direnv allow — trust a .envrc in this dir; auto-loads on cd. `layout mise` uses the local toolchain.
mkcert <host> — generate trusted local TLS certs. `mkcert -install` once per box first.
pre-commit install — wires the `.pre-commit-config.yaml` to .git/hooks/pre-commit.

# ── kubernetes / infra ─────────────────────────────────────────────
k9s — TUI for kubectl. `:` to command, `/` to filter, `?` for keybinds.
k — alias for kubectl. `tf` for terraform.
flux get all — top-level "what's flux reconciling" view.

# ── tmux ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmux: prefix is C-a. `|` splits right, `-` splits down. `h/j/k/l` to navigate.
tmux: prefix + r reloads ~/.tmux.conf. prefix + [ enters copy mode (vi keys).
tmux: tmux-resurrect saves session on Ctrl+a Ctrl+s, restores on Ctrl+a Ctrl+r.

# ── nvim ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
nvim: leader is Space. <leader>ff find files, <leader>fg live grep, <leader>fb buffers.
nvim: <leader>e toggles file tree. <leader>gg opens lazygit inside nvim.
nvim: K shows LSP hover docs. gd jumps to definition. <leader>rn renames symbol.

# ── zed ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
zed . — open the current dir in Zed (reuses the existing window). Config lives in ~/.config/zed, managed by chezmoi.
zed: cmd+shift+p opens the command palette; `zed: open default settings` shows every option with docs.
zed: extensions in ~/.config/zed/settings.json → auto_install_extensions. Add a line, push, every box gets it.

# ── ghostty ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ghostty: cmd+enter toggles fullscreen. cmd+d / cmd+shift+d split. cmd+h/j/k/l nav.
ghostty +list-keybinds — show every active binding (defaults + customs).
ghostty +list-themes — preview every bundled theme. Yours is "Catppuccin Mocha".

# ── atuin / shell history ─────────────────────────────────────────
atuin — Ctrl+R for fuzzy history search synced across every box.
atuin stats — interesting summary of your shell usage (most-run, busiest day, etc.).
atuin key — print the encryption key for backup. Lose it, lose access to synced history.

# ── restic / backup ───────────────────────────────────────────────
restic snapshots — list every backup snapshot in your repo. `--host=$(hostname)` for just this box.
restic stats latest — size of the latest snapshot.
restic restore latest --target /tmp/restore — pull files back from the latest backup.
~/.local/bin/restic-backup — run a backup right now (else 04:32 nightly).

# ── vps: tailnet tools (*.ts.skenmy.com) ──────────────────────────
home.ts.skenmy.com — Glance, the VPS front door: a link to every service plus live numbers. Start here if you forget what's running.
*.ts.skenmy.com hosts only route over Tailscale. If one won't load, run `tailscale status` before blaming the service.
links.ts.skenmy.com — linkding bookmarks. Settings → Integrations has a bookmarklet to save any page in one click.
rss.ts.skenmy.com — Miniflux RSS reader. j/k to move, v opens the original article, ? lists every shortcut.
watch.ts.skenmy.com — changedetection.io: watch any web page for changes. Alerts land on the ntfy `watch` topic.
tools.ts.skenmy.com — IT-Tools: JWT decode, base64, UUIDs, cron parser, regex tester, all offline. Not tools.skenmy.com (that's the Twitch login gate).
code.ts.skenmy.com — VS Code in the browser. Clone repos into its workspace; /opt/skenmy-vps is deliberately not mounted.
git.ts.skenmy.com — Forgejo: hourly pull-mirrors of every skenmy repo. The origin to clone from when GitHub is down. SSH is on port 2222.
grafana.ts.skenmy.com — metrics dashboards + alert rules. Provisioned from skenmy-vps/observability/grafana, so change them by PR.
dozzle.ts.skenmy.com — live logs for every container in the browser. The "what is it doing right now" view.
logs.ts.skenmy.com — VictoriaLogs: search past container logs with LogsQL, e.g. `_time:1h error`. The "what happened at 03:00" view.
healthchecks.ts.skenmy.com — Healthchecks dashboard (dead-man's switch for cron jobs). Shows which scheduled job went quiet.

# ── vps: public apps ──────────────────────────────────────────────
z.skenmy.com — Zipline file + screenshot host. Share links are public; uploads need your API token. 95MB max (Cloudflare caps at 100).
gist.skenmy.com — Opengist pastebin. Every gist is a git repo, so `git clone` works on any gist URL.
skenmy.com/admin — URL-shortener admin. Every slug becomes skenmy.com/<slug>.
status.skenmy.com — Gatus: public uptime for every host on the VPS. Embedded as the Status app in skenOS.
analytics.skenmy.com — Umami: privacy-friendly analytics for skenmy.com and friends.
fares.skenmy.com — fares-tracker: GWR fare-drop calendar.
tools.skenmy.com — Twitch login gate for the lowerthird / esaquiz / blockbuster / schedule control panels. Grants are managed here.
lowerthird + esaquiz: /control.html is behind the Twitch gate; source.html stays open so OBS browser sources can load it.
skenmy.com/notes — the Obsidian vault, published by notes-builder. Old notes.skenmy.com links redirect there.
daemon.skenmy.com — DAEMON, the bullet-hell game from skenOS, standalone and linkable.

# ── vps: alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
ntfy.skenmy.com topics: alerts (Gatus + Grafana, forwarded to Telegram), images (Diun image updates), watch (changedetection).
ntfy publish: curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -d "deploy done" https://ntfy.skenmy.com/<topic>. Anonymous access is denied, so a token is required.
Dead-man's switch for any job: `long-job && curl -fsS -m 10 --retry 3 https://hc.skenmy.com/ping/<uuid>`. Append /start before or /fail on error.

# ── vps: operating the box ────────────────────────────────────────
ssh deploy@vps-uk — VPS shell (tailnet + key only). root@vps-uk for host-level work. Never hand-edit /opt/skenmy-vps; deploys overwrite it.
./compose logs --tail=50 -f <svc> — on the VPS, always use ./compose, never bare `docker compose` (it misses services.d + env.d).
./bin/lint-stack — run in skenmy-vps before pushing. Catches missing DNS records, healthchecks, Gatus checks and backup labels.
New VPS service: services.d/<name>.yml + conf.d/<NN>-<host>.caddy + DNS record + Gatus check, then open a PR. Merging to main deploys it.
./bin/backup --check — preview what tonight's restic → B2 run will send. ./bin/restore --list / --fetch to pull a snapshot without touching live data.
sudo ./bin/reconcile-host --check — report VPS host drift (swap, patching, firewall) without changing anything.
sudo ./bin/firewall-trial --disable — the escape hatch if the VPS nftables rules ever lock SSH out.
Mac Mini CI: `runs-on: [self-hosted, linux, container]` puts a private repo's job on the desk Mac instead of spending GitHub minutes.
